;; THE SCRIPTED ANSWERS THIS TREE'S CHANGE ALTERS, against the base the guard
;; is given (test/change-stream-guard.sc). One entry per answer:
;; (label "why"), label the script's verb, or read-usage for read with no
;; arguments. The guard requires every observed difference to be listed and
;; every listed one to be observed, so an item that means to change a
;; scripted answer lists it here in the same commit, and the entry comes out
;; when that change is in the base.
((describe "read's usage gains [\"--ast\"] and its description a sentence on it: the body of a block the markdown projection writes, as a markdown tree, each reference carrying its live target")
 (read-usage "read's usage gains [\"--ast\"]: read with no arguments answers the usage form, which names the new option"))
